[src/rbtree.c](src/rbtree.c) now has:

**The node type** — `typedef enum { RED, BLACK } rb_color_t;` and `struct rb_node` with `key / value / left / right / parent / color`.

**`rb_insert` descent** ([src/rbtree.c:41-67](src/rbtree.c#L41-L67)):
```c
while (cur != NULL) {
	cmp = strcmp(key, cur->key);
	if (cmp == 0) { /* overwrite path -- TODO */ return -1; }
	parent = cur;
	cur = (cmp < 0) ? cur->left : cur->right;
}
```
Exits with `parent` = future parent of the new node and `cmp` = which side. Loop has its invariant comment. `cmp == 0` (key exists) is detected and stubbed for the overwrite slice; the empty-tree case falls through with `parent == NULL`.

The `(void)parent` / `(void)value` at the bottom are placeholders so it compiles under `-Werror` — they disappear in the next slice (`node_alloc` → link red child → `t->size++` → `insert_fixup`).

**Battery:** `make test` and `make asan` compile clean and run. `make memcheck` still can't run here (no valgrind). Not committing yet — partial, and nothing tests it.

