```

Same shape as the `rb_insert` descent, minus tracking `parent`. `make test` and `make asan` both clean.

This is the first thing that lets you actually exercise `rb_insert`/`insert_fixup` from outside the file — right now nothing calls either of them. Worth writing a real test next (insert a few keys, `rb_find` them back) before adding more surface area, since that's the only way to catch a rotation bug instead of just "it compiles."

