418	 * Returns the black-height of the subtree at n (NIL counts as black, so an
419	 * empty subtree is height 1); clears *ok the first time any rule breaks,
420	 * but keeps walking so the rest of the tree -- ordering included -- is
421	 * still checked. *prev is the previously-visited (in-order) node, so keys
422	 * can be compared as strictly increasing. */
